r a lost campaign record. During this wave's re-seeding an over-broad retire routine destroyed one historical record (2cc1df1b85c75d4940c2c62b7a19eea9b43ecd359878cf577de279793601f850), and recovery had to be performed ad hoc: the surviving plan snapshot reproduced the manifest hash EXACTLY (an identity proof) and the surviving completion outbox supplied the wave statuses and attempt counts. A rebuild-campaign! that reconstructs identity from the snapshot, reconciles statuses from the outbox and refuses on a plan-id mismatch would make this routine instead of forensic. See .planning/campaigns/INCIDENT-2cc1df1b-record-loss.md.")) #hasheq((classification . "deferred-noncritical") (owner . "W6 owner (adversarial permanence rehearsal)") (rationale . "F2-F10 reproduction fixtures in the W0 register harness read their recorded fields instead of recomputing, because they reference the unmerged W4 branch ce13d038 and live GitHub API responses that do not exist in the tree; only F1 executes live. W6 exercises these rows for real by replaying each injected defect through the W1-W5 guards.")) #hasheq((classification . "noncritical") (owner . "W1 owner (invocation-contract enforcement)") (rationale . "tests/test-wave-delivery-integrity-register.rkt's status-vocabulary comment says the vocabulary 'contains no passing value at all' while the list explicitly includes guarded-pass. The property that matters - an unguarded row can only be reported unguarded - does hold; only the wording is self-contradictory.")) #hasheq((classification . "noncritical") (owner . "W2 owner (evidence identity and digest integrity)") (rationale . "Two fidelity gaps in the W0 register harness: (a) it does not cross-check each reproduction's owning-wave against its register row (one fixture per row, expect=refused and the guard-status vocabulary are enforced; the data agrees by inspection F1->W1 ... F10->W3); (b) the contract-document check compares the four contract columns but not the document's Observed